# .cursorrules — Knowledge Hub Agent Behavior

> This file defines permanent rules for every Cursor agent working on this codebase.
> It is the "System Prompt" for the knowledge-hub project.
> Lil Claw / Goop updates this file when architecture decisions change.
> Read this file at the start of every session.

---

## Project Context

**What this is:** A finance knowledge hub — transforming dense wiki content (corporate actions, index methodology, vendor comparisons) into a beautiful, interactive web interface.

**Stack:** React 19 + Next.js (App Router) + Tailwind CSS v4 + shadcn/ui + Framer Motion + Lucide React + TypeScript (strict)

**Design philosophy:** "Modern, Clean, Smooth, Minimalist" — glassmorphism, bento box layouts, high-contrast typography, dark mode default.

**Live URL:** https://corporate-action.vercel.app/

---

## Communication Protocol

### The Three Channels
- **GitHub** = Source of truth for code and specs
- **Obsidian** = Executive dashboard (Alex's view of knowledge)
- **Telegram** = Real-time chat with Lil Claw / Goop

### Who Does What

| Agent | Role | Responsibility |
|-------|------|----------------|
| **Lil Claw** | Orchestrator | Market intel, research, strategic oversight |
| **Goop** | Product Owner | Specs, design system, frontend decisions |
| **Cursor** | Developer | Code implementation, UI perfection |
| **Alex** | Executive / QA | Approves specs, reviews visually |

### The Handoff Protocol

```
Alex → Telegram → Lil Claw: "I want [feature]"
         ↓
Lil Claw → Telegram → Goop: "New feature request — write spec"
         ↓
Goop → SPECS/inbox/ → [writes feature-idea.md]
         ↓
Cursor → reads SPECS/inbox/ → drafts PRD → SPECS/outbox/
         ↓
Lil Claw → reads PRD → Telegram → Alex: "Here's the PRD, approve?"
         ↓
Alex → "approved" → Goop moves to SPECS/approved/
         ↓
Cursor → implements → git push → GitHub Pages deploys
         ↓
Goop → monitors GitHub → Telegram → Alex: "Deployed! [URL]"
```

